-- SuperDirtGUI from Tidal - 39: the insert effects, played from Tidal
--
-- An insert of the sc fx kit family (Growl, Tunnel, Smear, Cloud, Stammer,
-- Sympathy, Spiral, the reverbs) can listen to Tidal: right click it in the
-- mixer, "listen to tidal" (or the check at the top of its own window). Its
-- slot turns green and shows its tidal name - growl, tunnel, growl2 ... -
-- which is now a sound: s "growl" plays nothing, it moves the Growl, by the
-- names its window shows in green. Or from SuperCollider, before this file:
--
--   g = ~sdg.addInsert(0, \growl); g.listening = true;
--   t = ~sdg.addInsert(1, \tunnel); t.listening = true;
--
-- The words (drive1, tone, feedback ...) are in boot.hs. n picks a preset; a
-- menu takes an item's name, or its index as a string ("3"). On a sound,
-- fx "growl" (...) moves the Growl with that sound. docs/sequencing-inserts.md
-- has the rest.

setcps (124/60/4)

-- a beat into orbit 0, where the Growl is
d1 $ s "[bd*4, ~ sn, hh*8]" # orbit 0

-- the drive in steps, on a pattern of its own
d9 $ s "growl*8" # drive1 "0 6 12 24 0 36 12 6"

-- or swept: a value every 16th
d9 $ s "growl*16" # drive1 (range 0 30 sine) # freq1 (range 300 4000 $ slow 4 saw)

-- the curve by name, a different one each bar
d9 $ s "growl" # type1 "<soft fold sine tube>"

-- a preset a bar: n wraps over the presets
d9 $ s "growl" # n "<0 1 3 6>"

-- with the sound itself: only the snare gets the wet growl
d1 $ stack [
    s "bd*4" # fx "growl" (mix 0),
    s "~ sn" # fx "growl" (mix 1 # tone 3000)
  ] # orbit 0

-- the lfos on the cycle. The wasp preset (6) has lfo 1 moving stage 1's
-- filter; its sync menu: free, four, two, one, half, quarter, eighth,
-- sixteenth, third, sixth, twelfth (periods in cycles)
d9 $ s "growl" # n 6 # lfo1Sync "<quarter eighth third half>"

-- Tunnel on orbit 1: feedback building over four cycles, then let go
d2 $ s "~ cp ~ ~" # orbit 1

d8 $ s "tunnel*4" # feedback (slow 4 $ range 0.3 1.05 saw) # mix 0.6

hush
